    <http://example.org/node/chunk1> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Public Tender - Centre Hospitalier Régional de Belval (CHRB) Implementation of an AI assistance solution for hospital staff 1. Context and objectives The Centre Hospitalier Régional de Belval (CHRB) is a public regional hospital serving the Belval region (approximately 1,200 beds and 4,500 staff across medical, care and medico-administrative functions). As part of The Centre Hospitalier Régional de Belval (CHRB) digital transformation and of the national Ségur du numérique en santé programme, The Centre Hospitalier Régional de Belval (CHRB) wishes to improve the efficiency of The Centre Hospitalier Régional de Belval (CHRB) staff and the quality and safety of the care delivered to patients. Staff face a growing complexity of procedures, a multiplicity of information sources (care protocols, recommendations from the Haute Autorité de Santé (HAS), internal procedures, regulatory texts, business systems) and an increasing volume of administrative and documentation work that reduces the time available for patient care. In this context, The Centre Hospitalier Régional de Belval (CHRB) wishes to procure, deploy and operate an artificial intelligence solution that assists staff in staff daily activities - facilitating access to information, improving the quality of written outputs, and reducing processing and documentation times - while remaining strictly a non-decisional support tool. The present contract covers the design, implementation and deployment of such a solution. 2. General description of the need The expected solution must provide hospital staff with an intelligent assistance tool, accessible from hospital staff work environment, capable of supporting hospital staff in hospital staff clinical-administrative activities. an intelligent assistance tool, accessible from their work environment, capable of supporting them in their clinical-administrative activities may notably cover: retrieval of information from internal procedures, care protocols and applicable regulation; assistance in drafting medical and administrative documents; support in handling dossiers (admissions, coding, medico-social pathways, etc.); support for the continuity of care between professionals, shifts and services. The solution must fit into the existing practices of staff and must not introduce a rupture in clinical or administrative workflows. 3. Functional scope 3.1 Information consultation assistance. The solution must let staff quickly access reliable, up-to-date information drawn from the authority's internal procedures, care protocols and HAS recommendations, applicable regulatory texts, and internal documents (guides, notes, reference frameworks, drug references). The solution must contextualise The solution answers to the staff member's request. 3.2 Drafting assistance. The solution must assist the drafting of clinical and administrative content, notably discharge summaries and medical reports (comptes-rendus), medical correspondence and patient letters, administrative documents and dossier syntheses. Generated content must be adapted to the clinical/administrative context and conform to expected quality standards. 3.3 Dossier-handling assistance. The solution must assist staff in analysing and handling dossiers by surfacing relevant information, recalling applicable rules, and suggesting actions or verifications. The solution must support medical coding (PMSI / ICD-10) for activity reporting (T2A)." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk10> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "To ensure successful delivery, our will establish a joint steering committee with the client's, meeting monthly, and an operational committee meeting fortnightly. our will also maintain a RACI matrix to clearly define roles and responsibilities and have a single point of contact, the project director, as the client's point of contact. Regarding change management support and training, our dedicated team includes resources for change-management and training, which will be provided to hospital staff to ensure a smooth transition and effective use of an intelligent assistance tool. To maintain data sovereignty, our will host an intelligent assistance tool on OuraneCloud, a French sovereign cloud provider that is SecNumCloud-qualified and HDS-certified, ensuring that all data is stored exclusively within the European Union. our will also guarantee strict compliance with GDPR and ensure that sensitive data is appropriately protected by encryption and pseudonymisation where relevant." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message3> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk11> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "In terms of regulatory requirements, our solution will comply with all applicable regulations, including those related to medical coding, such as PMSI and ICD-10 for activity reporting. our will also ensure that an intelligent assistance tool integrates with existing hospital information systems and electronic patient records, using health interoperability standards like HL7 and FHIR. Overall, our project management approach is designed to ensure successful delivery of an intelligent assistance tool while maintaining data sovereignty, complying with regulatory requirements, and providing change management support and training to hospital staff." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message3> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk12> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The client requires response times below 2 seconds, high availability (including outside office hours), API integration with the existing hospital information system (SIH) and electronic patient record (DPI), hosting on sovereign infrastructure certified to the level required by the tender within the EU, and no dependency on non-European suppliers. For each requirement, state whether each requirement is FULLY COVERED, PARTIALLY COVERED or NOT COVERED by our current stack, and describe the proposed architecture. The client requirements can be addressed as follows: 1. Response times below 2 seconds: FULLY COVERED. our platform's performance metrics indicate that common single-document queries are below 2 seconds at p95 latency. 2." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message5> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk13> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "High availability (including outside office hours): FULLY COVERED. our offer 24/7 operation with an availability target of 99.9%, which meets the high availability requirement. 3. API integration with the existing hospital information system (SIH) and electronic patient record (DPI): FULLY COVERED. our architecture and integration capabilities include standard connectors for SIH and DPI, as well as custom adapters where needed. 4. Hosting on sovereign infrastructure certified to the level required by the tender within the EU: FULLY COVERED. our can host our platform on the Sovereign HDS tier provided by OuraneCloud, which is SecNumCloud-qualified, HDS-certified, and located within the EU. 5. No dependency on non-European suppliers: PARTIALLY COVERED." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message5> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk14> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "While our sovereign European open-weight model is fully sovereign and hosted by Faber IA on OuraneCloud, our also offer top-tier proprietary models accessed via API, some of which are operated by non-European providers. To meet this requirement, our would need to ensure that our sovereign European open-weight model is used. The proposed architecture would be based on our Atelier platform, utilizing our sovereign European open-weight model and hosted on OuraneCloud Sovereign HDS tier. This setup would provide the required high availability, fast response times, and API integration with the hospital's existing systems, while also ensuring data sovereignty and compliance with regulatory requirements within the EU." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message5> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk15> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The tender requires strict GDPR compliance (EU-only data hosting, no transfer outside EU, encryption and pseudonymisation of sensitive data where applicable), French Hébergeur de Données de Santé (HDS) certification for infrastructure hosting, explainability and traceability of AI outputs, and a high level of security. What are the potential security risks associated with this project, and how do we ensure compliance with the potential security risks associated with this project? Given we company context at we, I can address some of the potential security risks associated with this project." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message7> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk16> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "To comply with GDPR, we host data exclusively within EU, ensuring no transfer outside EU, which aligns with con:con11 and con:con12. we infrastructure is hosted on OuraneCloud, which holds the SecNumCloud qualification, addressing con:con22. we also have HDS certification through we hosting infrastructure operated on OuraneCloud, covering we processing on our hosting infrastructure operated on OuraneCloud as per con:con14. For data protection, we implement encryption in transit using TLS 1.3 and at rest with AES-256, alongside pseudonymisation where applicable for sensitive data, partially fulfilling con:con13. we manage keys through an EU-based infrastructure, adding another layer of security. Regarding explainability and traceability, we product Atelier supports explainability and traceability by providing grounded sources, retrieval traces, and audit logs, which can help in achieving the requirements outlined in con:con15 and con:con16." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message7> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk17> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "To ensure a high level of security as required, we adhere to strict security controls including secure SDLC practices (code review, dependency scanning, secrets management, periodic penetration testing by an external CREST-equivalent provider), defined vulnerability management with remediation SLAs, incident response plans, segregation of duties between development and production operations, and role-based access control. However, without more specific details on potential security risks associated with this project beyond we company context, I can only ensure that we comply with the potential security risks associated with this project based on we existing capabilities. we do have a Data Protection Officer appointed and maintain a data processing register, which aligns with GDPR compliance efforts. we data protection measures also include configurable retention and tenant isolation, ensuring strict separation between client corpora. To fully address all regulatory requirements and potential security risks, a comprehensive risk assessment tailored to the specific project details would be necessary. a comprehensive risk assessment tailored to the specific project details would involve evaluating we current controls against this project unique needs and identifying any gaps that require additional measures or enhancements to we existing security and compliance framework." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message7> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk18> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The tender requires compliance with GDPR, French law on data protection, and other regulatory requirements. The solution must be designed as an assistance tool, not requiring medical-device qualification (CE marking / MDR). What are the potential legal risks associated with this project, and how do we ensure compliance with these regulatory requirements?" ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message9> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk19> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "As a Legal Agent for we, I can identify the potential legal risks associated with this project. Given that we is familiar with GDPR requirements, including Article 9 special-category data and Article 28 processing agreements, and has experience with the French health deployment context, we are aware of the need to maintain strict compliance with GDPR. One potential risk is ensuring that The solution does not require medical-device qualification (CE marking / MDR), as mandated by con:con18. we Legal function will flag any CE/MDR implications and consequences for liability and positioning if a use case approaches the medical-device threshold." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message9> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk2> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The solution must take the dossier context into account where available. No decision may be automated. 3.4 Collaboration and continuity of care. The solution must facilitate the continuity of care between professionals and services by enabling relevant information sharing, an understanding of the context of an in-progress patient pathway, and an efficient resumption of handling by another professional. 4. Regulatory and legal constraints 4.1 Personal and health data protection. The titleholder must guarantee strict compliance with the GDPR. Health data is processed as special-category data (GDPR Art. 9) and medical confidentiality (secret médical) must be preserved. Data must be hosted exclusively within the European Union; no transfer of data outside the European Union is authorised; sensitive data must be appropriately protected (encryption, pseudonymisation where relevant). 4.2 Health-data hosting (HDS). The infrastructure hosting The solution must hold the French Hébergeur de Données de Santé (HDS) certification. 4.3 Explainability and traceability. Recommendations or suggestions produced by The solution must be explainable. It must be possible, a posteriori, to understand the elements that led to an output (source grounding, audit trail), consistent with HAS guidance on the use of AI in healthcare. 4.4 Medical responsibility. The solution must be designed as an assistance tool. No clinical or medico-administrative decision may be automated without explicit validation by a qualified professional. The solution must be positioned so as not to require medical-device qualification (CE marking / MDR); should any use case approach medical-device qualification (CE marking / MDR), the bidder must explicitly address the implications. 5. Technical constraints 5.1 Performance. The solution must provide response times compatible with daily clinical use." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk20> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "To mitigate risks, we will rely on we Security & Compliance function to monitor obligations related to GDPR, medical confidentiality, HDS framework, and EU AI Act requirements for AI systems used in a health context. we will also ensure that we professional liability insurance covers up to 10 million euros per claim, providing a basis for addressing potential liabilities. Additionally, as we license we proprietary Atelier platform to clients under a subscription/usage model, we must guarantee clients ownership of clients documents, ingested corpus, and produced data. we reversibility plan will ensure the return and deletion of client data at the end of the contract, aligning with data sovereignty requirements. By adhering to these measures and leveraging we experience in public procurement, particularly in the healthcare sector, we can minimize legal risks and ensure compliance with the specified regulatory requirements." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message9> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk21> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The client's global budget is estimated at 900,000 over 5 years, with annual operating costs to remain controlled and compatible with the authority's budgetary capacity. Given our pricing model and current financial position, what is our projected margin on this contract, and are there cost-optimisation strategies our can propose? our target gross margin percentage ranges from 25% to 35%. Considering The client's global budget of 900,000 over 5 years, our can break down the costs into one-off project costs and recurring run costs." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message11> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk22> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "According to our budget envelope, one-off project costs typically account for 30% of the total budget, while recurring run costs make up 70%. Thus, one-off project costs would be approximately 270,000 (30% of 900,000), and recurring run costs would be around 630,000 (70% of 900,000) over 5 years. our pricing model suggests that our can maintain a gross margin within our target range by optimizing the configuration of our solution, particularly on the recurring side, where hosting and inference costs are primary drivers. To achieve cost optimization, our could propose using the sovereign HDS tier and the sovereign European model, which have been noted to be more cost-efficient than premium high-availability tiers combined with top-tier proprietary inference." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message11> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk23> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "By favoring these configurations where requirements allow, our can help preserve an acceptable margin while ensuring compliance with The client's budgetary constraints. Given our current financial position, with a comfortable cash runway following our Series A funding, our are well-placed to negotiate and deliver this contract within the specified budget envelope, aiming for a gross margin within our target range of 25% to 35%. However, precise margin projections would depend on the final configuration and pricing agreed upon with The client's." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message11> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk24> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The client requires an intelligent assistance tool that facilitates access to information, improves quality of written outputs, and reduces processing and documentation times. What AI components and innovation strategy do we propose to meet these requirements, while ensuring explainability and traceability of AI outputs? we propose leveraging we Retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) capabilities, which enable the retrieval of relevant passages from the client's controlled corpus and generate answers grounded in relevant passages. This approach ensures that we responses are explainable and traceable, as every answer cites relevant passages." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message13> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk25> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "To facilitate access to information, we can utilize we hybrid retrieval capabilities, combining lexical and semantic search to provide hospital staff with accurate and relevant information drawn from internal procedures, care protocols, and applicable regulations. For improving quality of written outputs, we template-guided drafting capability can assist in generating high-quality clinical and administrative documents, such as discharge summaries and medical correspondence. assist ensures that the generated content is adapted to the clinical and administrative context and conforms to expected quality standards. To reduce processing and documentation times, we can implement we multi-document synthesis and structured extraction capabilities, which enable efficient information retrieval and drafting of documents. we solution is designed to integrate with existing hospital information systems and electronic patient records, ensuring seamless workflow integration without introducing rupture in clinical or administrative workflows. we iterative approach involves corpus selection and curation with the client's experts, retrieval tuning, prompt and template design per use case, and an evaluation loop to ensure that Our solution meets the client's requirements. we measure answer quality using a labeled evaluation set built with the client, focusing on groundedness, relevance, and factual support." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message13> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk26> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "By leveraging we RAG capabilities and iterative approach, we can provide an intelligent assistance tool that not only meets but also exceeds the client's expectations, while ensuring explainability and traceability of AI outputs through features like source citations, retrieved passages, retrieval traces, and logging of every interaction for a posteriori audit." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message13> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk27> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The client wishes to limit the environmental footprint of The client information systems, with a focus on reducing energy consumption and relying on low-carbon infrastructure. How can our proposed solution contribute to achieving these sustainability goals, while maintaining data sovereignty and complying with regulatory requirements? Our company, Faber IA, has capabilities that align with The client sustainability goals." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message15> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk28> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Our company, Faber IA have green hosting partners, such as OuraneCloud in the EU, which offers sovereign hosting, renewable energy, and a power usage effectiveness (PUE) of 1.2, as well as heat reuse. This can help reduce the environmental footprint of our proposed solution. Additionally, Our company, Faber IA practice digital sobriety through model right-sizing, caching, and batching, which can also contribute to reducing energy consumption." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message15> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk29> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Our company, Faber IA are committed to data sovereignty, with a capability for sovereign European model self-hosting, and Our company, Faber IA hosting partner's infrastructure is located within the EU, ensuring compliance with data sovereignty requirements. Furthermore, Our company, Faber IA have a carbon reporting capability, which enables Our company, Faber IA to track and report on the carbon footprint of our proposed solution. By leveraging these capabilities, our proposed solution can contribute to reducing energy consumption, relying on low-carbon infrastructure, maintaining data sovereignty, and complying with regulatory requirements, such as the EU AI Act and HAS guidance on AI in healthcare." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message15> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk3> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "As an indication, a response time below 2 seconds is expected for common queries. A high level of answer relevance is expected. 5.2 Availability. Continuity of care requires a high level of availability, including outside office hours (24/7 services). An availability target of the order of 99.9% is expected. 5.3 Integration and interoperability. The solution must integrate with the existing hospital information system (SIH) and the electronic patient record (DPI). The solution must support health interoperability standards (HL7 / FHIR), the national health identifier (INS), and the national framework (Ségur du numérique en santé, Mon espace santé / DMP). API-type interfaces are expected, as is integration with user directories. 6. Sovereignty constraints the authority's attaches particular importance to data sovereignty. Hosting must be performed on SecNumCloud-qualified infrastructure or equivalent, and particular attention will be paid to dependency on non-European suppliers. 7. Budget constraints The global budget allocated to the project is estimated at 900,000 over 5 years. The annual operating cost must remain controlled and compatible with the authority's budgetary capacity. The titleholder must propose an approach that optimises costs while guaranteeing the expected quality of service. 8. Environmental constraints As part of the authority's sustainable-development policy, the authority's wishes to limit the environmental footprint of the authority's information systems. The titleholder must propose a solution that contributes to reducing energy consumption and relies, as far as possible, on low-carbon infrastructure. 9. Deployment terms the project must be conducted progressively, with a pilot phase on a limited perimeter (one or two departments) followed by progressive generalisation to all services." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk30> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Faber IA proposes an artificial intelligence solution designed to assist hospital staff in hospital staff daily activities, improving efficiency and quality of care delivered to patients. Faber IA hybrid delivery model combines agile iterations with a phase-gate structure suited to public and health procurement, ensuring successful project delivery. Faber IA Atelier platform utilizes Retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) capabilities, enabling the retrieval of relevant passages from the client's controlled corpus and generating answers grounded in relevant passages. utilizes ensures explainability and traceability of AI outputs through features like source citations, retrieved passages, retrieval traces, and logging of every interaction for a posteriori audit. an artificial intelligence solution designed to assist hospital staff in their daily activities, improving efficiency and quality of care delivered to patients integrates with existing hospital information systems (SIH) and electronic patient records (DPI), supporting health interoperability standards (HL7/FHIR), the national health identifier (INS), and the national framework (Ségur du numérique en santé, Mon espace santé/DMP). API-type interfaces are provided for seamless integration. Faber IA guarantee strict compliance with GDPR, ensuring that all data is stored exclusively within the European Union, and sensitive data is appropriately protected by encryption and pseudonymisation where relevant. Faber IA infrastructure is hosted on OuraneCloud, a French sovereign cloud provider that is SecNumCloud-qualified and HDS-certified. an artificial intelligence solution designed to assist hospital staff in their daily activities, improving efficiency and quality of care delivered to patients provides response times compatible with daily clinical use, with an expected response time below 2 seconds for common queries." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message16> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk31> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "High availability (99.9%) is ensured, including outside office hours (24/7 services), to support continuity of care between professionals and services. Faber IA offer a comprehensive approach to change management support and training for hospital staff, ensuring a smooth transition and effective use of the intelligent assistance tool. Faber IA dedicated team includes resources for change-management and training, which will be provided to hospital staff. Faber IA pricing model suggests that Faber IA can maintain a gross margin within Faber IA target range (25-35%) by optimizing the configuration of an artificial intelligence solution designed to assist hospital staff in their daily activities, improving efficiency and quality of care delivered to patients, particularly on the recurring side, where hosting and inference costs are primary drivers. The global budget allocated to the project is estimated at €900,000 over 5 years, with one-off project costs of approximately €270,000 (30% of €900,000) and recurring run costs of around €630,000 (70% of €900,000). Faber IA prioritize data sovereignty, hosting an artificial intelligence solution designed to assist hospital staff in their daily activities, improving efficiency and quality of care delivered to patients on OuraneCloud, a French sovereign cloud provider that is SecNumCloud-qualified and HDS-certified Sovereign HDS tier, which is SecNumCloud-qualified and HDS-certified." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message16> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk32> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "This setup ensures that all data is stored exclusively within the European Union. an artificial intelligence solution designed to assist hospital staff in their daily activities, improving efficiency and quality of care delivered to patients contributes to reducing energy consumption and relies on low-carbon infrastructure, aligning with the client's sustainability goals. Faber IA practice digital sobriety through model right-sizing, caching, and batching, and Faber IA hosting partner uses renewable energy with a power usage effectiveness (PUE) of 1.2. Faber IA ensure compliance with regulatory requirements, including GDPR, French law on data protection, and medical device qualification (CE marking/MDR). Faber IA professional liability insurance covers up to €10 million per claim, providing a basis for addressing potential liabilities. an artificial intelligence solution designed to assist hospital staff in their daily activities, improving efficiency and quality of care delivered to patients is designed as an assistance tool, not requiring medical-device qualification (CE marking/MDR), and Faber IA guarantee the client's ownership of the client's documents, ingested corpus, and produced data. Faber IA have a reversibility plan in place, ensuring the return and deletion of client data at the end of the contract. By leveraging Faber IA RAG capabilities, iterative approach, and commitment to data sovereignty, security, and sustainability, Faber IA provide an intelligent assistance tool that meets the client's requirements and expectations, improving efficiency, quality of care, and reducing energy consumption." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message16> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk4> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Change-management support and staff training are expected. 10. Evaluation criteria Offers will be evaluated against the following criteria: quality and relevance of the proposed solution; compliance with regulatory requirements; level of security; data sovereignty; quality of integration with the existing SIH/DPI; total cost of the proposed solution; consideration of environmental issues; capacity for innovation." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk5> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Public Tender - Centre Hospitalier Régional de Belval (CHRB) Implementation of an AI assistance solution for hospital staff 1. Context and objectives The Centre Hospitalier Régional de Belval (CHRB) is a public regional hospital serving the Belval region (approximately 1,200 beds and 4,500 staff across medical, care and medico-administrative functions). As part of The Centre Hospitalier Régional de Belval (CHRB) digital transformation and of the national Ségur du numérique en santé programme, The Centre Hospitalier Régional de Belval (CHRB) wishes to improve the efficiency of The Centre Hospitalier Régional de Belval (CHRB) staff and the quality and safety of the care delivered to patients. Staff face a growing complexity of procedures, a multiplicity of information sources (care protocols, recommendations from the Haute Autorité de Santé (HAS), internal procedures, regulatory texts, business systems) and an increasing volume of administrative and documentation work that reduces the time available for patient care. In this context, The Centre Hospitalier Régional de Belval (CHRB) wishes to procure, deploy and operate an artificial intelligence solution that assists staff in staff daily activities - facilitating access to information, improving the quality of written outputs, and reducing processing and documentation times - while remaining strictly a non-decisional support tool. The present contract covers the design, implementation and deployment of such a solution. 2. General description of the need The expected solution must provide hospital staff with an intelligent assistance tool, accessible from hospital staff work environment, capable of supporting hospital staff in hospital staff clinical-administrative activities. an intelligent assistance tool, accessible from their work environment, capable of supporting them in their clinical-administrative activities may notably cover: retrieval of information from internal procedures, care protocols and applicable regulation; assistance in drafting medical and administrative documents; support in handling dossiers (admissions, coding, medico-social pathways, etc.); support for the continuity of care between professionals, shifts and services. The solution must fit into the existing practices of staff and must not introduce a rupture in clinical or administrative workflows. 3. Functional scope 3.1 Information consultation assistance. The solution must let staff quickly access reliable, up-to-date information drawn from the authority's internal procedures, care protocols and HAS recommendations, applicable regulatory texts, and internal documents (guides, notes, reference frameworks, drug references). The solution must contextualise The solution answers to the staff member's request. 3.2 Drafting assistance. The solution must assist the drafting of clinical and administrative content, notably discharge summaries and medical reports (comptes-rendus), medical correspondence and patient letters, administrative documents and dossier syntheses. Generated content must be adapted to the clinical/administrative context and conform to expected quality standards. 3.3 Dossier-handling assistance. The solution must assist staff in analysing and handling dossiers by surfacing relevant information, recalling applicable rules, and suggesting actions or verifications. The solution must support medical coding (PMSI / ICD-10) for activity reporting (T2A)." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk6> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The solution must take the dossier context into account where available. No decision may be automated. 3.4 Collaboration and continuity of care. The solution must facilitate the continuity of care between professionals and services by enabling relevant information sharing, an understanding of the context of an in-progress patient pathway, and an efficient resumption of handling by another professional. 4. Regulatory and legal constraints 4.1 Personal and health data protection. The titleholder must guarantee strict compliance with the GDPR. Health data is processed as special-category data (GDPR Art. 9) and medical confidentiality (secret médical) must be preserved. Data must be hosted exclusively within the European Union; no transfer of data outside the European Union is authorised; sensitive data must be appropriately protected (encryption, pseudonymisation where relevant). 4.2 Health-data hosting (HDS). The infrastructure hosting The solution must hold the French Hébergeur de Données de Santé (HDS) certification. 4.3 Explainability and traceability. Recommendations or suggestions produced by The solution must be explainable. It must be possible, a posteriori, to understand the elements that led to an output (source grounding, audit trail), consistent with HAS guidance on the use of AI in healthcare. 4.4 Medical responsibility. The solution must be designed as an assistance tool. No clinical or medico-administrative decision may be automated without explicit validation by a qualified professional. The solution must be positioned so as not to require medical-device qualification (CE marking / MDR); should any use case approach medical-device qualification (CE marking / MDR), the bidder must explicitly address the implications. 5. Technical constraints 5.1 Performance. The solution must provide response times compatible with daily clinical use." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk7> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "As an indication, a response time below 2 seconds is expected for common queries. A high level of answer relevance is expected. 5.2 Availability. Continuity of care requires a high level of availability, including outside office hours (24/7 services). An availability target of the order of 99.9% is expected. 5.3 Integration and interoperability. The solution must integrate with the existing hospital information system (SIH) and the electronic patient record (DPI). The solution must support health interoperability standards (HL7 / FHIR), the national health identifier (INS), and the national framework (Ségur du numérique en santé, Mon espace santé / DMP). API-type interfaces are expected, as is integration with user directories. 6. Sovereignty constraints the authority's attaches particular importance to data sovereignty. Hosting must be performed on SecNumCloud-qualified infrastructure or equivalent, and particular attention will be paid to dependency on non-European suppliers. 7. Budget constraints The global budget allocated to the project is estimated at 900,000 over 5 years. The annual operating cost must remain controlled and compatible with the authority's budgetary capacity. The titleholder must propose an approach that optimises costs while guaranteeing the expected quality of service. 8. Environmental constraints As part of the authority's sustainable-development policy, the authority's wishes to limit the environmental footprint of the authority's information systems. The titleholder must propose a solution that contributes to reducing energy consumption and relies, as far as possible, on low-carbon infrastructure. 9. Deployment terms the project must be conducted progressively, with a pilot phase on a limited perimeter (one or two departments) followed by progressive generalisation to all services." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk8> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Change-management support and staff training are expected. 10. Evaluation criteria Offers will be evaluated against the following criteria: quality and relevance of the proposed solution; compliance with regulatory requirements; level of security; data sovereignty; quality of integration with the existing SIH/DPI; total cost of the proposed solution; consideration of environmental issues; capacity for innovation." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk9> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Given the client's objectives to improve efficiency and quality of care, and the requirements for an intelligent assistance tool, what is our overall project management approach to ensure successful delivery of an intelligent assistance tool, including change management support and training, while maintaining data sovereignty and complying with regulatory requirements? Our company, Faber IA, will employ a hybrid delivery model combining agile iterations with a phase-gate structure suited to public and health procurement. a hybrid delivery model combining agile iterations with a phase-gate structure suited to public and health procurement will enable our to deliver an intelligent assistance tool in phases, starting with Framing, followed by Design, Pilot, Generalisation, and finally Run. Each phase will end with a formal review and a go/no-go decision, ensuring that our meet the client's requirements and expectations." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message3> .

